{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-107491","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173330","text":"SpecPrompt — Open Standard for Spec-Driven AI Development"}]},{"id":"blk-107492","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173331","text":"Open standard and toolchain for spec-driven AI development. Defines a Markdown-based specification format (SPEC.md) that is human-readable and machine-parseable."}]},{"id":"blk-107493","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173332","text":"The landing page is GENERATED. Do not hand-edit "},{"id":"spn-173333","marks":["code"],"text":"index.html"},{"id":"spn-173334","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-107494","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173335","marks":["code"],"text":"/index.html"},{"id":"spn-173336","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173337","marks":["code"],"text":"/derive.js"},{"id":"spn-173338","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-173339","marks":["code"],"text":"/form.js"},{"id":"spn-173340","text":" are emitted by "},{"id":"spn-173341","marks":["code"],"text":"build-site.mjs"},{"id":"spn-173342","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-173343","marks":["code"],"text":"records/surface.json"},{"id":"spn-173344","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173345","marks":["code"],"text":"src/landing.html"},{"id":"spn-173346","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173347","marks":["code"],"text":"src/shell.css"},{"id":"spn-173348","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173349","marks":["code"],"text":"src/derive.js"},{"id":"spn-173350","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-173351","marks":["code"],"text":"src/form.js"},{"id":"spn-173352","text":". "},{"id":"spn-173353","marks":["bold"],"text":"An edit to the served HTML is silently reverted by the next build."},{"id":"spn-173354","text":" Change the record or the template."}]},{"id":"blk-107495","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"./site.sh     # run the suite(s), emit the site, run the publication gate"},{"id":"blk-107496","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173355","marks":["code"],"text":"build-site.mjs"},{"id":"spn-173356","text":" does not quote a test count — it "},{"id":"spn-173357","marks":["bold"],"text":"executes"},{"id":"spn-173358","text":" the suite, parses what the runner prints, and refuses to emit anything if a number has moved off "},{"id":"spn-173359","marks":["code"],"text":"records/tests.json"},{"id":"spn-173360","text":". That is how the count on this page stopped being a thing anyone could type."}]},{"id":"blk-107497","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173361","marks":["code"],"text":"launch-gate.mjs"},{"id":"spn-173362","text":" reads the emitted artifact and refuses to publish when it and the records disagree: a retracted claim reinstated, a rung invented, a CTA the rung has not earned, an unrendered token, a "},{"id":"spn-173363","marks":["code"],"text":"mailto:"},{"id":"spn-173364","text":" or an email address, a text token below 4.5:1, a same-origin link that resolves to nothing, an artifact that is not what this build emitted, an identifying-animation constant leaking into the copy, or a button whose colour is decided by a non-button rule. "},{"id":"spn-173365","marks":["bold"],"text":"It prints its own total"},{"id":"spn-173366","text":" &mdash; 115 on 2026-08-17, and that figure is the only one in this repository that is not derived, which is why it carries a date. "},{"id":"spn-173367","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not hand-type a check count anywhere:"},{"id":"spn-173368","text":" it went from 92 to 115 in a single session, and a typed count is exactly how a printed number and a published one drift apart."}]},{"id":"blk-107498","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173369","text":"Built against "},{"id":"spn-173370","marks":["bold"],"text":"`shell-r9`"},{"id":"spn-173371","text":", recorded as "},{"id":"spn-173372","marks":["code"],"text":"shell_revision"},{"id":"spn-173373","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-173374","marks":["code"],"text":"records/surface.json"},{"id":"spn-173375","text":". The whole shell is documented in "},{"id":"spn-173376","marks":["code"],"text":"ProjectAmp2/agents/SHELL.md"},{"id":"spn-173377","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-107499","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173378","marks":["bold"],"text":"The band says \"a specification in the ComputeDriven world\", not \"the specification layer of ComputeDriven\", and that is deliberate."},{"id":"spn-173379","text":" "},{"id":"spn-173380","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand-nav"},{"id":"spn-173381","text":" records this domain as "},{"id":"spn-173382","marks":["code"],"text":"place: 3"},{"id":"spn-173383","text":", whose "},{"id":"spn-173384","marks":["code"],"text":"renderPlacement()"},{"id":"spn-173385","text":" gives the layer sentence to "},{"id":"spn-173386","marks":["code"],"text":"place: 2"},{"id":"spn-173387","text":" only. The old eyebrow claimed the layer and is now blocklisted."}]},{"id":"blk-107500","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173388","marks":["bold"],"text":"Contact is the Formspree endpoint ruled by Travis (SHELL.md r9)"},{"id":"spn-173389","text":", as a real "},{"id":"spn-173390","marks":["code"],"text":"<form>"},{"id":"spn-173391","text":" that posts with scripting off; "},{"id":"spn-173392","marks":["code"],"text":"src/form.js"},{"id":"spn-173393","text":" only upgrades it to an inline reply and prints success solely on a 2xx. No "},{"id":"spn-173394","marks":["code"],"text":"mailto:"},{"id":"spn-173395","text":" anywhere."}]},{"id":"blk-107501","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173396","text":"Source-of-truth spec"}]},{"id":"blk-107502","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107504","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173397","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-173398","text":" — SpecPrompt product specification"}]}],"id":"blk-107503","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107505","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173399","text":"Role in [&] Ecosystem"}]},{"id":"blk-107506","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173400","text":"SpecPrompt is the "},{"id":"spn-173401","marks":["bold"],"text":"standards layer"},{"id":"spn-173402","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-107507","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SpecPrompt (Standards) → Agentelic (Engineering) → OpenSentience (Runtime) → Graphonomous (Memory)"},{"id":"blk-107508","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173403","text":"SpecPrompt defines the interoperable format that bridges agent definition with execution, testing, and deployment."}]},{"id":"blk-107509","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173404","text":"The SPEC.md format"}]},{"id":"blk-107510","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173405","text":"Markdown files with YAML frontmatter. Required sections: Purpose, Capabilities, Constraints, Acceptance Tests. Human-readable, machine-parseable, git-versioned."}]},{"id":"blk-107511","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173406","text":"Toolchain"}]},{"id":"blk-107512","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107514","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173407","text":"CLI: validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile (--output/--approve/--status), diff, publish"}]}],"id":"blk-107513","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107516","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173408","text":"MCP server: 8 tools (spec_validate, spec_lint, spec_generate, spec_test_gen, spec_test_compile, spec_test_approve, spec_diff, spec_search)"}]}],"id":"blk-107515","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107518","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173409","text":"Reference parser in Elixir (TypeScript parser planned)"}]}],"id":"blk-107517","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107520","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173410","text":"Formal PEG grammar for conformant parser development"}]}],"id":"blk-107519","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107521","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173411","text":"Interoperability"}]},{"id":"blk-107522","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107524","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173412","text":"Bidirectional with Next Moca ADL ("},{"id":"spn-173413","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/interop/adl.ex"},{"id":"spn-173414","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-107523","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107526","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173415","text":"Bidirectional with ampersand.json ("},{"id":"spn-173416","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/interop/ampersand.ex"},{"id":"spn-173417","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-107525","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107528","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173418","text":"Complementary to AGENTS.md"}]}],"id":"blk-107527","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-107529","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173419","text":"Build commands"}]},{"id":"blk-107530","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"# Elixir\nmix deps.get\nmix compile --warnings-as-errors\nmix test\nmix format --check-formatted\nmix escript.build    # produces ./specprompt CLI\n\n# TypeScript parser\ncd npm && npm install && npm test"},{"id":"blk-107531","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-173420","text":"Status"}]},{"id":"blk-107532","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173421","text":"All 6 BUILD.md phases implemented. 93 tests (71 Elixir + 22 TypeScript), 0 failures."}]},{"id":"blk-107533","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107535","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173422","text":"Phase 1: Parser + Validator + Linter + Differ + CLI (validate, lint, diff)"}]}],"id":"blk-107534","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107537","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173423","text":"Phase 2: Test Compiler (compile prompts, approve, status) + Test Generator"}]}],"id":"blk-107536","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107539","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173424","text":"Phase 3: MCP Server (all 8 tools) + Publisher (CloudEvents)"}]}],"id":"blk-107538","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107541","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173425","text":"Phase 4: Supabase migration ("},{"id":"spn-173426","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand-supabase/migrations/100_spec_schema.sql"},{"id":"spn-173427","text":", "},{"id":"spn-173428","marks":["code"],"text":"101_spec_rls.sql"},{"id":"spn-173429","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-107540","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107543","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173430","text":"Phase 5: Registry CRUD ("},{"id":"spn-173431","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/registry.ex"},{"id":"spn-173432","text":" — Supabase client via :httpc)"}]}],"id":"blk-107542","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107545","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173433","text":"Phase 6: TypeScript parser ("},{"id":"spn-173434","marks":["code"],"text":"npm/"},{"id":"spn-173435","text":" — @specprompt/parser, identical output to Elixir parser)"}]}],"id":"blk-107544","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107547","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173436","text":"Interop: ampersand.json + ADL bidirectional mapping"}]}],"id":"blk-107546","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-107549","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-173437","text":"Deploy: Dockerfile + fly.toml"}]}],"id":"blk-107548","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierapfzpmdx4id2wvydtjnwb4zb4qzxiohzdj6jfu2krysnh3lhhydhq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}